    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(10201)_n=(n^2+1)^2$ for every integer base $n>2$.\n\nIts square root is $(101)_n$.",
      "worked": "Let the base be an integer $n>2$. Using place value,\n$$\\begin{align*}(10201)_n&=n^4+2n^2+1\\\\(10201)_n&=(n^2)^2+2(n^2)(1)+1^2\\\\(10201)_n&=(n^2+1)^2\\end{align*}$$\nSince $(101)_n=n^2+1$, the numeral $(10201)_n$ is the square of $(101)_n$ in every such base.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
